{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2134","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Even Larger"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"An array is called "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if, for every subarray$$$^{\\text{∗}}$$$ of length at least $$$2$$$, the sum of the elements at even indices (with respect to the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"original array"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":") is greater than or equal to the sum of the elements at odd indices. Array indexing starts from $$$1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, the arrays $$$[3,8,4,4]$$$ and $$$[2,3,1,4,2]$$$ are good. The array $$$[0,2,4,1]$$$ is not because, in the subarray $$$[2,4,1]$$$, the elements at even indices in the original array are $$$2$$$ (index $$$2$$$) and $$$1$$$ (index $$$4$$$), while the only element at an odd index is $$$4$$$ (index $$$3$$$). Since $$$2 + 1 \\lt 4$$$, the condition does "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"not"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" hold for this subarray."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an array of $$$n$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"non-negative"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers $$$a_1,a_2,\\ldots,a_n$$$. In one operation, you can decrease any element in the array by $$$1$$$, but all elements must remain "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"non-negative"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Your task is to find the minimum number of operations needed to make the array $$$a$$$ good. It can be proved that it is possible to make the array good using a finite number of operations."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^{\\text{∗}}$$$An array $$$b$$$ is a subarray of an array $$$a$$$ if $$$b$$$ can be obtained from $$$a$$$ by the deletion of several (possibly, zero or all) elements from the beginning and several (possibly, zero or all) elements from the end. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$). The description of the test cases follows. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2 \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — the length of the array $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains $$$n$$$ non-negative integers $$$a_1,a_2,\\ldots,a_n$$$ ($$$0 \\le a_i \\le 10^9$$$) — the elements of the array $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output a single integer in a new line — the minimum number of operations needed to make the array $$$a$$$ good."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n8\n4\n3 8 4 4\n4\n0 2 3 5\n2\n3 1\n5\n2 3 1 4 2\n4\n0 2 4 1\n5\n3 1 4 5 1\n11\n3 0 5 4 4 5 3 0 3 4 1\n12\n410748345 10753674 975233308 193331255 893457280 279719251 704970985 412553354 801228787 44181004 1000000000 3829103\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n0\n1\n2\n0\n3\n6\n14\n4450984776\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, the array $$$a$$$ is already good, so the answer is $$$0$$$. Below are the checks for each subarray:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Subarray"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Even Index Sum"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Odd Index Sum"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Condition met?"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$[3,8]$$$"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$8$$$"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$3$$$"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"chi